// are kept apart, in a small precise set the loop drives by the OS's
// high-resolution timer. A program makes one call, "wake me at this time",
// and the wheel decides which kind it is: anything due within a tick goes
// precise by itself. It is pure data: no threads, no waits, no OS. The
// completion loop (iocore, next) owns one per loop, waits in the OS until
// nextExpiry, and turns what expired hands it into completions.
//
//   mod loop;
//   import time use Duration, Instant, Clock;
